mono.vendor/patches/luau-lsp/codegen-null-logger-guards.patch

Make optional lowering diagnostics explicitly require their logger.

WHY THIS IS A PATCH
    Native compilation calls lowerImpl with a null LogBuilder and disabled text
    output. The routine already provides an empty string for that case, but its
    output branches only test AssemblyOptions. GCC 13's optimized build reports
    seven -Wnonnull warnings on the logger calls. Explicit logger guards keep
    native compilation silent and preserve assembly/IR output when a logger is
    supplied, without disabling warnings or removing language-server features.

WHERE IT GOES
    luau/CodeGen/src/CodeGenLower.h, in lowerImpl: the outputEnabled calculation,
    three includeIr blocks, and the trailing IR-prefix output condition.

WHEN IT STOPS APPLYING
    Re-point the five guards at lowerImpl's optional diagnostic-output branches.
    Remove this patch if upstream already makes those branches require a logger.
    scripts/vendor-tree.sh applies it to the copied nested Luau tree only and
    stops if upstream changes its preimage.

VALIDATION
    Rebuild through just typecheck-editor with warnings enabled and inspect the
    cold build log. Also verify native compilation without a logger, then request
    assembly and IR through getAssembly and check that both contain lowered code.

diff --git a/luau/CodeGen/src/CodeGenLower.h b/luau/CodeGen/src/CodeGenLower.h
--- a/luau/CodeGen/src/CodeGenLower.h
+++ b/luau/CodeGen/src/CodeGenLower.h
@@ -101,7 +101,7 @@ inline bool lowerImpl(
             bcLocations[irLocation] = uint32_t(i);
     }
 
-    bool outputEnabled = options.includeAssembly || options.includeIr;
+    bool outputEnabled = logger && (options.includeAssembly || options.includeIr);
 
     std::string emptyLog;
     IrToStringContext ctx{logger ? logger->text : emptyLog, function.blocks, function.constants, function.cfg, function.vmExitInfo, function.proto};
@@ -138,7 +138,7 @@ inline bool lowerImpl(
             seenFallback = true;
         }
 
-        if (options.includeIr)
+        if (logger && options.includeIr)
         {
             if (options.includeIrPrefix == IncludeIrPrefix::Yes)
                 logger->formatAppend("# ");
@@ -168,7 +168,7 @@ inline bool lowerImpl(
         // Block might establish a safe environment right at the start
         if ((block.flags & kBlockFlagSafeEnvCheck) != 0)
         {
-            if (options.includeIr)
+            if (logger && options.includeIr)
             {
                 if (options.includeIrPrefix == IncludeIrPrefix::Yes)
                     logger->formatAppend("# ");
@@ -230,7 +230,7 @@ inline bool lowerImpl(
             // Either instruction result value is not referenced or the use count is not zero
             CODEGEN_ASSERT(inst.lastUse == 0 || inst.useCount != 0);
 
-            if (options.includeIr)
+            if (logger && options.includeIr)
             {
                 if (options.includeIrPrefix == IncludeIrPrefix::Yes)
                     logger->formatAppend("# ");
@@ -283,7 +283,7 @@ inline bool lowerImpl(
             }
         }
 
-        if (options.includeIr && options.includeIrPrefix == IncludeIrPrefix::Yes)
+        if (logger && options.includeIr && options.includeIrPrefix == IncludeIrPrefix::Yes)
             logger->formatAppend("#\n");
 
         if (block.expectedNextBlock == ~0u)
